<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saidu Sharif</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Saidu Sharif is a town in the Swat valley of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-west-frontier-province">Khyber Pakhtunkhwa</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a>, beside the larger town of Mingora. It grew around the shrine of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akhund-of-swat">Akhund of Swat</a> and became the capital of the princely state of Swat under his descendants, the Walis, who built schools, hospitals and colleges there. It remains the administrative centre of Swat district.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/saidu-sharif.jpg" alt="Saidu Sharif" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Isruma · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saidu_Sharif_-2012.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
